# Allow-list, not deny-list: exclude everything, then re-include exactly
# what the Dockerfile copies. A deny-list grows a hole every time a new
# local file appears; this does not.

*

# What the build actually needs
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!rustopnsmcp/
!rustopnsmcp-core/

# Re-exclude sensitive and generated paths that live *inside* those
# directories. A later pattern wins, so these override the re-inclusions
# above.
**/target/
**/tokens.json
**/*.tokens.json
**/devices.json
**/*.opnsensekey
**/.opnsensekey
**/.opnsense-api-key
**/.opnsense-api-secret
**/.env
**/.env.*
